Clearcote optional build-host adapter: use the actual CLT macOS SDK for host tools

Why: Chromium 150's sdk_info.py requires xcodebuild, and find_sdk.py assumes
Xcode.app's SDK directory layout. Apple's Command Line Tools has a usable SDK
and compiler/linker, but no Xcode application/version or platform directory.
Use scripts/mac_clt_sdk.py copied into the private build tree by
scripts/prepare_mac_clt.py, only for local non-official Mac -> Windows builds.
Xcode version stays unavailable (empty/0); the CLT package/provider/version and
actual SDK version/build are recorded explicitly. No system tools are wrapped
or modified, and no fake Xcode.app/version plist is created.

This is an opt-in host-build compatibility patch, not a browser privacy patch.
It remains separate from the mandatory Clearcote patches/series. The complete
series and its L1 gate must still be applied and retained unchanged.

